## Pile of playing cards
// a drawable list:  each pile is its own element, <drawable-solitaire-pile>, holding its cards' elements
a pile is a drawable list of cards:
	<css>
		:host {
			display: block;
			position: relative;
			min-height: 30px;
		}
		.pile {
			position: relative;
			min-height: 30px;
		}
		/* its cards, stacked:  the last on top */
		::slotted(*) {
			position: absolute;
			left: 0;
			top: 0;
			width: 100%;
		}
		.placeholder {
			box-sizing: border-box;
			height: 30px;
			border: 1px dashed #b0b0b0;
			border-radius: 4px;
			text-align: center;
			cursor: pointer;
		}
		.placeholder.red {
			color: crimson;
		}
		.placeholder .suit {
			font-size: 1.4rem;
			line-height: 28px;
		}
	</css>
// a card is in one pile at a time:  putting it on another pile takes it off this one
a card belongs to one pile
a pile has a name as text

the color of a pile is:
	if it is empty return "none"
	return the color of its last card

the value of a pile is:
	if it is empty return 0
	return the value of its last card

the state of a pile is:
	set state to (the name of the pile or "pile") + ":"
	for each card in pile
		set state to state + " " + the state of the card
	return state
